(f) The rate contract shall be entered into for price, without commitment for quantity and time of supply of the subject-matter of procurement, with the bidder of the lowest riced bid or most advantageous bid fulfilling the laid down eligibility and qualification criteria including past performance against such rate contract, availability of ISI mark or service centres across the State and such other criteria as required and these conditions as applicable shall be specified in the bidding documents;
(g) The procuring entity shall also reserve its right to conclude parallel rate contacts with different bidders, in addition to the responsive bidder submitting the lowest priced bid or most advantageous bid, but at the rates of such bidder;
(h) That, in case the price quoted by the lowest responsive bidder is not reasonable or found to be high, the price may be negotiated with lowest responsive bidder with whom the rate contract may be concluded consequent only upon lowering of the bid price to the desired level.
